                <pb facs="0329" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7008: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-07T12:00:00+08:00">June 7, 1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The transfer of Yu Hsueh-chung from his post as chairman of Hopei Province to
                    that of Bandit Suppression Commander for the Szechuan, Shansi and Kansu border
                    is officially confirmed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
